     <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
     <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
     <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
+
     <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
     <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
     <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
+    <p>We follow the principle of data minimization: we only collect what a feature needs to work, and only when you use that feature. This Data Protection Declaration explains exactly which data we collect, where it goes, and the purposes we use it for.</p>
+
     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+
+    <h3 id="cookies">Cookies</h3>
+    <p>Reading articles does not set any cookies. We use a single first-party cookie, <code>astro-session</code>, and only after you save an article to your reading list. It contains a random identifier that links your browser to your saved list on our server. It is <code>HttpOnly</code> (scripts cannot read it), is sent only to this website, and contains no other information. You can remove it at any time by clearing your browser's cookies for this site.</p>
+
+    <h3 id="analytics">Click analytics</h3>
+    <p>To understand which links and buttons are useful, we load a small analytics script from our content service (<code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>). When you click a link or button, it records only:</p>
+    <ul>
+        <li>the type of element clicked (link or button),</li>
+        <li>the visible text of that element, and</li>
+        <li>the time of the click.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>It does not set cookies, does not record what you type, and neither the script request nor the click reports include the address of the page you are reading (at most our domain name). As with any web request, the service necessarily receives your IP address.</p>
+    <p>The analytics script and advertising slots are <strong>never</strong> loaded on the sign-in and sign-up pages. If your browser sends a <a href="https://globalprivacycontrol.org/">Global Privacy Control</a> signal, we treat it as an opt-out and do not load the analytics script or advertising slots on any page.</p>
+
+    <h3 id="accounts">Accounts</h3>
+    <p>Creating an account requires only a username and a password. You don't need to use your real name or email address. When you sign up or sign in, these are sent over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection directly to our account service and are used only to create your account and sign you in. The request does not include cookies or the address of the page you came from, and the sign-in and sign-up pages are marked so that they are not stored in shared caches.</p>
+
+    <h3 id="third-parties">Fonts and other third-party resources</h3>
+    <p>All fonts are served from this website. We do not load fonts or other resources from third-party font or CDN providers, so your IP address is not shared with them when you view a page.</p>
+
+    <h3 id="browser-features">Browser features</h3>
+    <p>This website does not use your camera, microphone, location, or motion sensors, and instructs your browser to block these features for the site and any embedded content. We also opt out of the browser's Topics API for interest-based advertising. When you follow a link to another website, your browser only tells that website our domain name, not the specific page you were reading.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
